397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Regional climate variations The climate can vary somewhat between the northern and southern parts of Brittany. The northern coast, including areas such as Saint-Malo and Brest, tends to experience more frequent rainfall and stronger winds due to its exposure to the Atlantic Ocean. In contrast, the southern part of Brittany, including regions around Vannes and Lorient, benefits from slightly drier conditions and more stable weather patterns. Coastal areas generally have milder winters and cooler summers compared to the more inland regions, which can experience more temperature fluctuations.)
/E (Regional climate variations The climate can vary somewhat between the northern and southern parts of Brittany. The northern coast, including areas such as Saint-Malo and Brest, tends to experience more frequent rainfall and stronger winds due to its exposure to the Atlantic Ocean. In contrast, the southern part of Brittany, including regions around Vannes and Lorient, benefits from slightly drier conditions and more stable weather patterns. Coastal areas generally have milder winters and cooler summers compared to the more inland regions, which can experience more temperature fluctuations.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
